    {
      "name":  "PopRm16",
      "comment": "0x8F /0 POP r/m16. Other 8F /N (1..7) are invalid on 8086 — modrm.reg is dispatched at decode time but we only register /0 here; invalid /N would silently take this path (acceptable since they're undefined on 8086 anyway).\n\nNote 0xFF /6 PUSH r/m16 deliberately omitted from 24.6.5f because the FF group contains 8 different opcode-extension variants (/0=INC, /1=DEC, /2=CALL near, /3=CALL far, /4=JMP near, /5=JMP far, /6=PUSH, /7=invalid). They will be added together in 24.6.7 when CALL/JMP indirect land.",
      "fields": {},
      "mask":  "0xFF",
      "match": "0x8F",
      "instructions": [
